This is a plain COPY of the live desktop dotfiles, not a live one -- nothing
here is managed, symlinked, or read by Home Manager. It exists purely as a
version-controlled backup. Editing a file in here does nothing to your actual
running config; edit the real file under ~/.config or ~ instead, then re-copy
here if you want the backup updated.

Deliberately left out of Phase 7/8 of the Nix migration (see the main
README) -- this is the live matugen-driven theming + Hyprland/quickshell
setup, and Home Manager taking it over declaratively would fight matugen and
the compositor for control of files they actively regenerate.

config/   copies of ~/.config/{hypr,waybar,kitty,rofi,swaync,wlogout,foot,
          matugen,fastfetch,qt5ct,qt6ct,cava}
home/     copies of ~/.p10k.zsh, ~/.gtkrc-2.0, ~/.aliases
boot/     Plymouth + GRUB theme sources, copied from ~/Downloads/archplys
          (archply1/arch-mac-style = active Plymouth theme, archply2/
          arch-slider-and-glow = the other installed Plymouth theme, fluent =
          the active GRUB theme). plymouthd.conf says which Plymouth theme is
          active (Theme=arch-mac-style); grub-theme-setting.txt is the
          GRUB_THEME line from /etc/default/grub. To actually reinstall
          either: Plymouth themes go in /usr/share/plymouth/themes/<name>/,
          then `sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R <name>`; GRUB theme goes
          in /usr/share/grub/themes/<name>/, set GRUB_THEME in
          /etc/default/grub, then `sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg`.

Known exclusion: config/hypr/scripts/quickshell/calendar/.env had a real
OpenWeather API key in it. Removed from this copy, replaced with
.env.example (a template). The real key stays only in the live,
untracked ~/.config/hypr/scripts/quickshell/calendar/.env. If you ever want
this properly secret-managed instead of sitting in plaintext, it's a good
candidate for the agenix setup in modules/secrets.nix.
